Application Type: Provisional Patent Application

TECHNICAL FIELD

This invention relates to artificial intelligence systems for compliance gap analysis and regulatory assessment, specifically utilizing machine learning algorithms and natural language processing for automated evaluation of organizational compliance status against regulatory requirements.

BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION

Organizations across all industries face complex regulatory compliance requirements that require continuous monitoring, assessment, and gap analysis. Traditional compliance assessment methods rely on manual review processes that are time-intensive, subjective, and prone to human error.

Current compliance management systems can track compliance status but lack intelligent analysis capabilities to identify specific gaps, prioritize remediation efforts, and provide actionable recommendations for achieving compliance. Manual compliance assessments are costly, inconsistent across assessors, and cannot scale to handle complex regulatory frameworks with hundreds of requirements.

Aviation training organizations, for example, must comply with FAR Part 142 requirements involving over 200 checklist items across 10 inspection areas. Manual assessment of compliance against these requirements requires extensive regulatory expertise and cannot provide consistent, objective gap analysis across different organizations or assessment periods.

SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION

The present invention provides an intelligent compliance gap analysis system that uses artificial intelligence to automatically assess organizational compliance status, identify specific gaps, prioritize remediation efforts, and generate actionable recommendations for achieving regulatory compliance.

The system utilizes advanced natural language processing and machine learning algorithms to analyze uploaded documents, correlate them with specific regulatory requirements, and provide multi-dimensional compliance assessment with confidence scoring and risk stratification.

Key innovations include:
- AI-powered document correlation with specific regulatory checklist items
- Multi-dimensional compliance assessment with confidence scoring
- Automated risk stratification and priority assignment for compliance gaps
- Actionable recommendation generation for compliance achievement
- Continuous learning and improvement through user feedback integration

